Senior Structural Assembly Manufacturing Engineer &lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Electra&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Air travel is about to become something more: more direct, more accessible, and more connected to the places where people live, work and want to be. Every day in the U.S., people make 35 million trips of 50–500 miles, stuck in traffic or routed through crowded hubs. Chances are, you&#39;ve been one of them. At Electra, we&#39;re changing that with the EL9, a nine-passenger, hybrid-electric aircraft that takes off and lands in just 150 feet. Our Ultra Short technology opens up thousands of new places to fly, beyond conventional runways, congested airports and long drives. We&#39;re backed by Lockheed Martin, Honeywell and Safran. Operators worldwide have signed intent-to-purchase agreements for the first 2,200 aircraft we produce, and we&#39;re moving toward first test flights in 2027.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Getting a new kind of aircraft airborne takes more than ambition. It takes our kind of bold: people who think big while working in the real world. Who move ideas into action and collaborate without silos. Who put people first and make room at the table for everyone. Who challenge one another without diminishing one another.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Sound like you? Then look beyond what you thought were your own limits, and help us take flight beyond runways.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Electra&#39;s Senior Structural Assembly Manufacturing Engineer, you&#39;ll play a key role in developing and industrializing the structural assembly processes for the EL9 aircraft, working from early product development through prototype build, production implementation, and ramp-up.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll work closely with Product Engineering during aircraft development to ensure structural designs incorporate Design for Manufacturing and Assembly (DFMA) principles and can be efficiently, repeatably, and reliably produced. You&#39;ll bring a hands-on manufacturing perspective to structural design decisions, evaluating assembly sequence, tolerance management, access, tooling, fastening and joining methods, inspection requirements, producibility, and production risk.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the EL9 transitions from design into physical hardware, you&#39;ll help translate released engineering into executable manufacturing processes and support prototype and initial aircraft builds. You&#39;ll work closely with airframe manufacturing suppliers, providing on-site Manufacturing Engineering oversight and liaison support as needed to ensure proper information flow, resolve technical and quality issues, support the incorporation of product changes and support supply chain on contract management.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is an opportunity to influence both how the aircraft is designed and how it is ultimately built, while helping establish Electra&#39;s structural assembly manufacturing supply chain capability from the ground up.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product Engineering throughout aircraft development to ensure structural designs incorporate Design for Manufacturing and Assembly (DFMA) principles and support efficient, repeatable, and scalable production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review aircraft structural designs, assemblies, drawings, models, and engineering changes from a manufacturing perspective, providing recommendations related to producibility, assembly sequence, access, tolerance stack-up, fastening and joining methods, tooling, inspection, and production risk.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in design trade studies, concept reviews, and design reviews, representing Manufacturing Engineering and identifying manufacturing constraints and opportunities early in the development cycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide Manufacturing Engineering oversight and liaison support at airframe and structural suppliers, working directly with supplier manufacturing teams to clarify design and manufacturing intent, resolve producibility and assembly issues, and maintain program execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with the airframe supplier Tooling Engineering to define assembly tooling concepts, requirements, locating strategies, interfaces, and implementation plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review supplier manufacturing approaches, build plans, assembly processes, tooling concepts, and production readiness to ensure alignment with Electra&#39;s engineering requirements and program objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support prototype fabrication, development aircraft assembly, first builds, and production implementation, providing hands-on Manufacturing Engineering support to resolve issues encountered during structural assembly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate technical resolution of manufacturing issues and nonconformances with Product Engineering, Stress, Quality, Supplier Quality, Supply Chain, and other stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Capture manufacturing lessons learned and supplier feedback from prototype and initial production builds and drive those learnings back into product design, manufacturing processes, tooling, and planning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support structural assembly production ramp-up by identifying constraints, resolving manufacturing issues, improving assembly processes, and driving improvements in quality, cost, schedule, and production rate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to the development and continuous improvement of Electra manufacturing engineering standards, methods, processes, and best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Mechanical, Aerospace, Aeronautical, Manufacturing Engineering, or a related engineering field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of aerospace manufacturing engineering experience, with significant experience in aircraft structural assembly and industrialization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong hands-on knowledge of aircraft structural assembly processes, including metallic and/or composite airframe structures, drilling, fastening, joining, shimming, sealing, alignment, and major structural integration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience applying Design for Manufacturing and Assembly (DFMA) principles during aircraft product development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience reviewing engineering drawings, 3D models, GD&amp;amp;T, tolerances, and engineering changes from a manufacturing and assembly perspective.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing manufacturing plans, assembly sequences, work instructions, tooling requirements, and manufacturing engineering documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting prototype, development, or first-production aircraft builds.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working directly with aircraft structures suppliers or manufacturing partners and supporting production activities in a factory environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to work effectively across Product Engineering, Stress, Quality, Supplier Quality, Supply Chain, Tooling, and Production organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong problem-solving skills and ability to make sound engineering recommendations in a fast-moving aircraft development environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to work effectively across internal teams and external suppliers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability and willingness to travel to supplier and manufacturing locations as required by program needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Points&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with clean-sheet aircraft development and transition from prototype into production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with major structural assemblies such as fuselage, wing, empennage, control surfaces, or other primary airframe structures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with aircraft assembly tooling, jigs, fixtures, determinant assembly, or advanced assembly methodologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with digital manufacturing tools, PLM/MES environments, manufacturing BOMs, and 3D model-based manufacturing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with supplier industrialization, production readiness assessments, or manufacturing capability reviews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with MRB, root cause corrective action, and production nonconformance resolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with AS9100 aerospace quality management systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;This range reflects the anticipated hiring range across all eligible locations; actual compensation is determined based on your relevant experience, skills, and geographic location. Total compensation includes performance bonus and comprehensive benefits.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Compensation Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$130,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$155,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Medical, dental, and vision insurance; STD, LTD, and life insurance&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Generous PTO, sick leave, and company holidays&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Paid winter break&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;401(k) with immediate vesting&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Free catered lunches, coffee, snacks, and drinks at our Manassas headquarters&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Free on-site parking&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Electra is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. This position may be subject to ITAR requirements.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a> Manufacturing & Tech  Olten, Solothurn

Director, Solutions Architecture EMEA &lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Nebius:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nebius is leading a new era in cloud infrastructure for the global AI economy. We are building a full-stack AI cloud platform that supports developers and enterprises from data and model training through to production deployment, without the cost and complexity of building large in-house AI/ML infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Built by engineers, for engineers. From large-scale GPU orchestration to inference optimization, we own the hard problems across compute, storage, networking and applied AI.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Listed on Nasdaq (NBIS) and headquartered in Amsterdam, we have a global footprint with R&amp;amp;D hubs across Europe, the UK, North America and Israel. Our team of 1,500+ includes hundreds of engineers with deep expertise across hardware, software and AI R&amp;amp;D.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;The role&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As we continue to scale our business across EMEA, we are looking for an experienced&lt;strong&gt; Director, Solutions Architecture EMEA&lt;/strong&gt; to lead our customer-facing Solutions Architecture organization across the region.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a leadership role responsible for building, developing and scaling a high-performing Solutions Architecture organization across multiple countries and markets. You will partner closely with EMEA Sales leadership, establish the operating model for the regional team, and ensure our Solutions Architects consistently deliver outstanding technical leadership and business value to customers. The scope of the role reflects where the business is today; as we scale, we expect the organization to specialize and subdivide, and this leader will help shape and staff that evolution.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for an experienced people leader who can build and empower strong teams while remaining close to customers, technology and our most strategic opportunities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’re welcome to work remotely from &lt;strong&gt;Europe&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-charstyle=&quot;Strong&quot;&gt;Your responsibilities will include:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:true}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build, lead and coach a high-performing Solutions Architecture team across multiple countries and markets in EMEA&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the Solutions Architecture engagement model for EMEA in close partnership with regional Sales leadership, including how coverage and ownership are divided as the team expands&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish clear priorities, operating mechanisms and performance expectations across the regional Solutions Architecture organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and scale the organization as the business grows, including hiring, coaching and developing senior technical professionals and future leaders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage directly with CIOs, CTOs, Heads of Infrastructure, Heads of AI/ML, Business leaders and other senior stakeholders across strategic customers and partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion the voice of EMEA customers internally and provide guidance for Nebius&#39;s Product and Technology roadmap&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-charstyle=&quot;Strong&quot;&gt;We expect you to have:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:true}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven &lt;strong&gt;people-management experience&lt;/strong&gt;, including hiring, coaching and developing senior technical professionals and leaders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong track record of &lt;strong&gt;leading customer-facing technical teams across EMEA&lt;/strong&gt;, with experience managing teams distributed across multiple countries and markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience building, scaling and operating regional Solutions Architecture, Sales Engineering, Customer Engineering or similar technical organizations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong &lt;strong&gt;player-coach mentality&lt;/strong&gt; with the ability to operate effectively at both leadership and execution levels — from organizational strategy and talent development to direct engagement in strategic customer opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of the EMEA technology market and the ability to operate effectively across different countries, cultures, customer segments and levels of market maturity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to operate effectively across both the &lt;strong&gt;technical and business dimensions&lt;/strong&gt; of complex customer engagements and influence C-level and senior stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent executive communication, presentation and stakeholder-management skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to operate effectively in a fast-growing environment where team structures, coverage boundaries and scope of ownership will continue to evolve&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-charstyle=&quot;Strong&quot;&gt;It will be an added bonus if you have:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:true}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of cloud-native infrastructure, including compute, storage, networking, security and Kubernetes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leadership experience within a &lt;strong&gt;public cloud, hyperscaler or rapidly scaling cloud infrastructure organization&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with &lt;strong&gt;GPU-based infrastructure workloads and accelerated computing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing or supporting &lt;strong&gt;machine learning and AI workloads&lt;/strong&gt;, including training and inference&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of distributed AI/ML infrastructure and the compute, networking and storage considerations associated with large-scale GPU workloads&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Kubernetes-based AI/ML platforms, MLOps or AI infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience helping customers evaluate the economics of large-scale compute or GPU workloads &lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;#LI-PL1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits &amp;amp; Perks:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive compensation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Career growth and learning opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexibility and ownership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative and innovative culture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Opportunity to work on impactful AI projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;International environment and talented teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What&#39;s it like to work at Nebius:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fast moving&amp;nbsp;- Bold thinking&amp;nbsp;- Constant growth&amp;nbsp;- Meaningful impact&amp;nbsp;- Trust and real ownership&amp;nbsp;- Opportunity to shape the future of AI&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal Opportunity Statement:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nebius is an equal opportunity employer. We are committed to fostering an inclusive and diverse workplace and to providing equal employment opportunities in all aspects of employment. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy), national origin, ancestry, age, disability, genetic information, marital status, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Applicants must be authorized to work in the country in which they apply and will be required to provide proof of employment eligibility as a condition of hire.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you need accommodations during the application process, please let us know.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a> Solutions Architecture

Account Director (6 month FTC) &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This is a 6 month fixed term contract initially, with a strong likelihood of extention.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;DEPT® is a Growth Invention company built to help the world’s most ambitious brands grow faster. Operating at the intersection of technology and marketing, our 4,000+ specialists deliver growth invention services across Brand &amp;amp; Media, Experience, Commerce, CRM, and Technology &amp;amp; Data. We’re 50|50 tech and marketing, partner-led, and first to move. Clients include Google, Lufthansa, Meta, eBay, and OpenAI. We have been certified B Corp and Climate Neutral since 2021.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;JOB PURPOSE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;This role is part of our &lt;/em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Global Studios&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;em&gt; team. We create emotive yet conversion-focused ideas, products and campaigns at scale and speed. Our specialty is hyper-personalised, digital communications that change perceptions, shape new behaviours, and shift market share for our clients.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Account Director, you will be responsible for building strong relationships with clients at all levels including strategic input, and overseeing the delivery of a wide variety of substantial integrated campaigns.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be required to manage client briefs from start to finish, planning, assigning and reviewing creative and managing the overall agency workload in partnership with the producers and the senior design team.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be working closely with designers, copywriters, developers and other parts of the agency to ensure successful campaign deliveries which are profitable without compromising creative integrity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU’LL DO&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage client briefs from start to finish, ensuring successful delivery to client deadlines across multiple campaigns.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Liaise with clients and manage their expectations.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Re-lay client feedback to designers, copywriters and developers &amp;amp; plan and manage workloads of the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure client requirements are met whilst protecting DEPT® values/brand.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the senior team with administrative tasks.  &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a full understanding of the clients’ business, strategies, objectives, brand, audiences and challenges, advising on the communications solution that best meets their needs, with a view to becoming their trusted adviser.  &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build excellent working relationships with key clients – regular meetings, planning, briefing, evaluation.  &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with creative and strategy teams and to have oversight of all statements of work/proposals as well as all content production for clients.  &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure the right DEPT® team is in place to deliver, high standards are maintained and adding value wherever possible. Ensure success criteria are met and projects are delivered to time and to budget.  &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure a good knowledge of all DEPT® products and services and actively promote them to clients.  &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Report to senior management with internal and external issues and events that might impact upon accounts, either positively or negatively.  &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct account management activity – undertaking pitches and presentations, formulating and implementing account plans, and running the account management process.  &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hold key new business development responsibilities, working with others in the team to proactively seek new opportunities for the business. Writing proposals and creative treatment. Contributing to winning new business.  &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure processes are followed and that there is consistent professional delivery (to brief). Managing workflows. Lead Account Direction best practice within the Agency.  &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain a strategic overview of key accounts and their markets – running regular internal client-facing account reviews. To prove how we are meeting our clients’  objectives through metrics, feedback, research, etc.  &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee the client contract, to proactively manage the account and resources to maximise profitability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Management and leadership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Delegate and allocate responsibilities efficiently to manage projects end to end.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interview candidates and hire resources.  &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct performance reviews of team members and identify areas of improvement, give feedback and recommend for promotions or salary increments.  &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effectively lead teams and inspire others to achieve goals through innovation, quality and excellence.  &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify strengths and weaknesses of team members and suitably make changes if required.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Encourage team interaction, boost employee motivation and appreciate team contribution.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Match project tasks with opportunities for development so that employee potential is utilised to the maximum.  &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage change and effectively cascade information to teams to ensure smooth execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU BRING&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience delivering a broad range of multi-channel marketing communications including digital and direct.  &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extremely organised, with the ability to manage multiple projects simultaneously.  &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work under pressure and meet and manage deadlines with ease and efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent verbal and written communication skills. &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A great team player and team-building skills. &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;People management/leadership skills. &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent negotiator with good networking ability.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to communicate effectively with team giving guidance and feedback.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Resource management skills and ability to handle complex issues.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of the production &amp;amp; interactive processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent planning and organisation skills. &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to manage and develop client and supplier relationships.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to commercially manage budgets.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven business development experience and success. &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced working knowledge of Microsoft Office Packages. &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WE OFFER&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A flexible hybrid working policy to enjoy the best of both worlds (2 days from the office, depending on location).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Early Finish Fridays, kickstart your weekend early with alternating early-finish Fridays.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;26 days paid holiday, plus UK Bank Holidays.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Access to dedicated mental health resources including enhanced sick pay scheme, employee assistance programme and trained Mental Health First Aiders.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company Pension Scheme.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Access to a Private Medical Insurance or Cash Plan scheme.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Season Ticket Loan, interest-free Season Ticket Loans to help spread the cost of travel.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cycle to Work Scheme, save money on a new bike and equipment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;EV Car Scheme, access to an electric vehicle via a salary sacrifice arrangement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enhanced family-friendly policies to support parents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Workplace Nursery Scheme, save on childcare by paying for nursery fees through a tax-efficient salary sacrifice scheme.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;DEPT® Allowance, a dedicated company contribution to spend on either your professional development or personal wellbeing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Social and Cultural Events, plenty of opportunities to connect with colleagues through organised activities and celebrations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learning and Development, continuous growth opportunities through internal training, and &quot;inspirational talks” guest speakers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Buddy Program, you will be paired with a ‘Buddy’ to help you navigate your first weeks’ at DEPT®.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A Certified BCorp Agency and is multi-award winning “Agency of the Year”.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Awesome clients. Whether big or small, local or global, at DEPT® you’ll get the opportunity to work with clients of all sizes and across all industries. And we celebrate all of our successes together!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Global &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.deptagency.com/dept-cares-day-2023/&quot;&gt;DEPT® Cares Month&lt;/a&gt;, an annual initiative where our teams donate their professional skills and time to support local charities and pr-bono projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHY DEPT®?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are a Growth Invention company built to help the world’s most ambitious brands grow faster. Operating at the intersection of technology and marketing, we create what is next by pioneering ideas, acting fast, and moving further because standing still just is not in our DNA.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are drawn to people who stay curious, move with intent, and never stop inventing. Our culture runs on three values: better together, relentlessly curious, and get sh*t done. It is how we work, how we grow, and how we make things that matter.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At DEPT®, you will find the freedom to explore, the space to collaborate, and the trust to make a real impact for our clients, for each other, and for the world we are helping to build.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;DIVERSITY, EQUITY &amp;amp; INCLUSION&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At DEPT®, we take pride in creating an inclusive workplace where everyone has an equal opportunity to thrive. We actively seek to recruit, develop, nurture, and retain talented individuals from diverse backgrounds, with varying skills and perspectives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Not sure you meet all qualifications? Apply, and let us decide! Research shows that women and members of underrepresented groups tend not to apply for jobs when they think they may not meet every requirement, when in fact they do. We believe in giving everyone a fair chance to shine.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We also encourage you to reach out to us and discuss any reasonable adjustments we can make to support you throughout the recruitment process and your time with us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Want to know more about our dedication to diversity, equity, and inclusion? Check out our efforts &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.deptagency.com/the-good-company/&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a> Clients

Analytics Engineer &lt;h3 class=&quot;whitespace-pre-wrap break-words font-normal first:pt-0 last:pb-0&quot; data-pm-slice=&quot;0 0 []&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;inline-block&quot; data-name=&quot;orange_heart&quot; data-type=&quot;emoji&quot;&gt;🧡&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt; About Alma&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;whitespace-pre-wrap break-words font-normal first:pt-0 last:pb-0&quot;&gt;At Alma, we believe sustainable commerce depends on fair, well‑balanced trade. Because finance plays a pivotal role in business, our mission is to put it back in its rightful place - serving merchants and consumers. Our installment and deferred payment solutions help merchants boost sales by 20% or more, increase customer loyalty, and deliver a seamless shopping experience - without encouraging bad debt. As the buy now pay later leader in France and active in 10 European countries, we&#39;ve empowered over +25,000 merchants and 10 million consumers. With 400+ Almakers and €100M+ ARR, Alma is scaling rapidly across Europe as a member of the Next40, and we&#39;re just getting started!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;whitespace-pre-wrap break-words font-normal first:pt-0 last:pb-0&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;whitespace-pre-wrap break-words font-normal first:pt-0 last:pb-0&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;inline-block&quot; data-name=&quot;open_hands&quot; data-type=&quot;emoji&quot;&gt;👐&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt; About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;whitespace-pre-wrap break-words font-normal first:pt-0 last:pb-0&quot;&gt;You will join Alma’s central Data team, which supports a wide range of business teams, including Finance, Product, Marketing, Risk, and Operations. The team is made up of six Data Analysts, including several experienced colleagues, and works at the intersection of Data Engineering, Data Analytics, and business teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;whitespace-pre-wrap break-words font-normal first:pt-0 last:pb-0&quot;&gt;Reporting to &lt;a class=&quot;text-blue-600 hover:underline hover:text-blue-800&quot; href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/in/gilmarlard/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Gil Marlard&lt;/a&gt;, you will help strengthen the data foundations that support reporting, analytics, operational processes, and business decision-making.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;whitespace-pre-wrap break-words font-normal first:pt-0 last:pb-0&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;This position is a permanent (CDI) role based in Paris, with a hybrid working model, we are also open to full remote in France.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;whitespace-pre-wrap break-words font-normal first:pt-0 last:pb-0&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;whitespace-pre-wrap break-words font-normal first:pt-0 last:pb-0&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;inline-block&quot; data-name=&quot;briefcase&quot; data-type=&quot;emoji&quot;&gt;💼&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt; About the job&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;whitespace-pre-wrap break-words font-normal first:pt-0 last:pb-0&quot;&gt;As an Analytics Engineer, you will help strengthen the data foundations that support the whole organization. The central Data team serves a wide range of business teams, including Finance, Product, Marketing, Risk, and Operations. You will join a team of six Data Analysts, including several experienced colleagues, and work at the intersection of Data Engineering, Data Analytics, and business teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;whitespace-pre-wrap break-words font-normal first:pt-0 last:pb-0&quot;&gt;You will transform raw data into trusted datasets that support reporting, analytics, operational processes, such as deciding which customer to call, and business decision-making.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;whitespace-pre-wrap break-words font-normal first:pt-0 last:pb-0&quot;&gt;Our data foundations currently have different levels of maturity across business teams, and part of our ambition is to rebuild and standardize some of them. Your work will be particularly important in enabling more self-service and conversational analytics for our business teams, by making data easier to find, understand, trust, and use.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;whitespace-pre-wrap break-words font-normal first:pt-0 last:pb-0&quot;&gt;A key part of your role will be improving the lineage and governance of our tables, following a medallion-inspired approach with clear layers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data modeling and data quality&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;pb-2 flex flex-col gap-1 list-disc pl-6&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;break-words&quot;&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;whitespace-pre-wrap break-words font-normal first:pt-0 last:pb-0&quot;&gt;Build and maintain reusable data models, macros, and semantic layers in dbt and BigQuery&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;break-words&quot;&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;whitespace-pre-wrap break-words font-normal first:pt-0 last:pb-0&quot;&gt;Develop staging, intermediate, and mart models following clear data modeling principles&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;break-words&quot;&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;whitespace-pre-wrap break-words font-normal first:pt-0 last:pb-0&quot;&gt;Implement data quality tests, freshness checks, and documentation&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;break-words&quot;&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;whitespace-pre-wrap break-words font-normal first:pt-0 last:pb-0&quot;&gt;Improve the lineage, ownership, and discoverability of our most important tables&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;break-words&quot;&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;whitespace-pre-wrap break-words font-normal first:pt-0 last:pb-0&quot;&gt;Strengthen our semantic layer and ensure that metric definitions are consistent&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;break-words&quot;&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;whitespace-pre-wrap break-words font-normal first:pt-0 last:pb-0&quot;&gt;Identify and remove duplicated, obsolete, or deprecated datasets and content&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;break-words&quot;&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;whitespace-pre-wrap break-words font-normal first:pt-0 last:pb-0&quot;&gt;Optimize queries and models for reliability, performance, and cost&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Central Data Analytics Community&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;pb-2 flex flex-col gap-1 list-disc pl-6&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;break-words&quot;&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;whitespace-pre-wrap break-words font-normal first:pt-0 last:pb-0&quot;&gt;Build reusable data assets that can be leveraged by Data Analysts across different business domains&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;break-words&quot;&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;whitespace-pre-wrap break-words font-normal first:pt-0 last:pb-0&quot;&gt;Lead enablement by mentoring analysts and training them on dbt, Looker, governance, and metric definitions&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;break-words&quot;&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;whitespace-pre-wrap break-words font-normal first:pt-0 last:pb-0&quot;&gt;Partner on the data platform roadmap across GCP, BigQuery, Argo, dbt, and Looker&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;break-words&quot;&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;whitespace-pre-wrap break-words font-normal first:pt-0 last:pb-0&quot;&gt;Contribute to keeping our data stack clean, reliable, and easy to maintain&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;break-words&quot;&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;whitespace-pre-wrap break-words font-normal first:pt-0 last:pb-0&quot;&gt;Participate in code reviews and help define analytics engineering standards&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;break-words&quot;&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;whitespace-pre-wrap break-words font-normal first:pt-0 last:pb-0&quot;&gt;Discuss and validate data contracts with the rest of the Engineering team&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;break-words&quot;&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;whitespace-pre-wrap break-words font-normal first:pt-0 last:pb-0&quot;&gt;Collaborate with Data Analysts, Data Engineers, and business stakeholders to deliver trusted and actionable data&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;whitespace-pre-wrap break-words font-normal first:pt-0 last:pb-0&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;inline-block&quot; data-name=&quot;toolbox&quot; data-type=&quot;emoji&quot;&gt;🧰&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt; You will work with&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;whitespace-pre-wrap break-words font-normal first:pt-0 last:pb-0&quot;&gt;dbt, BigQuery, Looker, GCP, Argo, Git, Claude&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;whitespace-pre-wrap break-words font-normal first:pt-0 last:pb-0&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;whitespace-pre-wrap break-words font-normal first:pt-0 last:pb-0&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;inline-block&quot; data-name=&quot;jigsaw&quot; data-type=&quot;emoji&quot;&gt;🧩&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt; About you&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;whitespace-pre-wrap break-words font-normal first:pt-0 last:pb-0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;To succeed in this job&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;pb-2 flex flex-col gap-1 list-disc pl-6&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;break-words&quot;&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;whitespace-pre-wrap break-words font-normal first:pt-0 last:pb-0&quot;&gt;You have at least 2 years of experience in Analytics Engineering, Data Engineering, Data Analytics, or a similar role.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;break-words&quot;&gt;
